//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @page c_tafecall eCall Service
 *
 * @rst :ref:`API reference <File taf_ecall_interface.h>` @endrst
 *
 * @rst :ref:`HAL APIs <File tafHalECall.h>` @endrst
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 * eCall is a technology initiative intended to bring rapid assistance to automotive accidents
 * anywhere. When a serious vehicle accident occurs, sensors automatically trigger an eCall.
 * When activated, the in-vehicle system (IVS) establishes a voice connection to a Public Safety
 * Answering Point (PSAP). At the same time, a digital minimum set of data (MSD) message is sent
 * over the voice call using in-band modem signals. The MSD includes accident information like
 * time, location, driving direction, and vehicle description.
 * An eCall can also be triggered manually.
 * An emergency call is needed for applications that want to establish emergency communication
 * with a remote party. The emergency call can be over an emergency mobile network or VoIP.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_binding IPC interfaces binding
 *
 * All functions of the eCall API are provided by the @b tafECallSvc application service.
 * TafECallSvc allows users to start an eCall, talk/converse through an eCall, send MSD
 * information, and send location info to PSAPs.
 *
 * The following example illustrates how to bind to eCall services.
 *
 * @verbatim
   bindings:
   {
       clientExe.clientComponent.taf_ecall -> tafECallSvc.taf_ecall
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_operation eCall operation modes
 *
 * The modem can operate in three different eCall modes.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode() -- This API makes the eCall operating mode eCall only. Only emergency
 *   numbers should be used to start eCall sessions in this mode. The modem may not try to register
 *   with the cellular network. The modem is forced to behave as only eCalls are allowed regardless
 *   of the the U/SIM operation mode. This change persists through device reboot, i.e., power cycles.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_ForcePersistentOnlyMode() -- This function is deprecated and taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode()
 *   should be used instead.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_ExitOnlyMode() -- This function causes the device to exit eCall Only mode. It changes the
 *   eCall operation mode to Normal. Generally the modem applies the default operation mode at boot up
 *   (and after U/SIM hotswap). The modem acts following the U/SIM eCall operation mode. For example the
 *   U/SIM can be setup only for eCall or a combination of eCall and normal commercial service provision.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_GetConfiguredOperationMode() -- This function helps the user fetch the configured
 *   operation mode of the modem or NAD.
 *   The various operation modes can be:
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_MODE_NORMAL -- The modem acts as the U/SIM eCall operation mode.
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_MODE_ECALL -- eCall only mode as per U/SIM operation mode or forced by
 *                                  the application through the taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode() API.
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_MODE_FORCED_PERSISTENT_ONLY -- Deprecated.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_MsdVersion eCall MSD version
 *
 * MSD version can be set/got with:
 *  - taf_ecall_SetMsdVersion()
 *  - taf_ecall_GetMsdVersion()
 *
 * These configurations take effect at the next test eCall and currently only MSD version 2 and 3 are supported.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_session eCall session
 *
 * taf_ecall_Create() helps to create a new eCall object and returns a reference to the eCall session.
 * taf_ecall_GetType() is used to query the current type of the eCall session.
 * taf_ecall_IsInProgress() is used to query the eCall in progress or not.
 * At this point the eCall is not yet started, the eCall session must be started using one of the
 * following functions.
 * - taf_ecall_StartManual() -- Initiates a manual eCall session; triggered by a passenger
 * - taf_ecall_StartAutomatic() -- Initiates an automatic eCall session; triggered automatically
 *                                 by the IVS if there is an accident or emrgency.
 * - taf_ecall_StartTest() -- Initiates a test eCall session; mainly used to test the communication between
 *   the IVS and the PSAP
 *
 * - taf_ecall_StartPrivate() -- Initiates a private eCall session
 *
 * The eCall can be ended by calling taf_ecall_End().
 *
 * taf_ecall_Answer() is used to answer an incoming eCall when the minimum network registration
 * timer is active.
 *
 * @b WARNING: An application should wait for end of the existing eCall before dialing another
 *             with the @c taf_ecall_StartXxx() APIs. An eCall is stopped when any of the following occurs.
 *
 *             - The application successfully stops it with taf_ecall_End() returning @c LE_OK
 *             - The @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED event arrives
 *             - The @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_CLEAR_DOWN event is notified
 *             - The @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_FAILED event is notified and no redial is initiated
 *
 * If the eCall object is no longer required, the application can call taf_ecall_Delete() to free
 * all allocated resources of the eCall object.
 *
 * The current state of the eCall session may be queried by taf_ecall_GetState().
 * Apart from this, an application may register a state change handler to be notified when the
 * session state changes. The handler can be controlled using taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler()
 * and taf_ecall_RemoveStateChangeHandler().
 *
 * An application may call taf_ecall_GetTerminationReason() to get the end reason of the eCall
 * when the eCall state is @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED and and
 * taf_ecall_GetPlatformSpecificTerminationCode() to get the platform-related termination code.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_PsapNumber eCall number
 *
 * Depending on the operating mode, the standard eCall number is defined by the modem or read from
 * the USIM fixed dialing numbers/service dialing numbers (FDN/SDN).
 *
 * A third-party eCall number can be set/got with:
 *  - taf_ecall_SetPsapNumber()
 *  - taf_ecall_GetPsapNumber()
 * These configurations take effect at the next eCall.
 *
 * To request that the modem reads the number from FDN/SDN, call taf_ecall_UseUSimNumbers() before starting
 * an eCall.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_timer_configuration NAD eCall deregistration time
 *
 * Network Access Device (NAD), i.e. the modem, deregistration allows the device to remain
 * registered to the network for an amount of time after the eCall is ended, either remotely or
 * the user hangs up locally using taf_ecall_End().
 * The deregistration duration can be set using the taf_ecall_SetNadDeregistrationTime() API and
 * retrieved using the taf_ecall_GetNadDeregistrationTime() API.
 *
 * The taf_ecall_SetNadDeregistrationTime() API is used to set the time value of a
 * <em>deregistration timer</em> after an eCall ends, so that the NAD remains registered on the
 * network for a duration of time and then automatically deregisters from the network upon
 * expiration of the timer.
 *
 * Moreover, when NAD (i.e. Modem) is in <b>eCall Only</b> mode and an eCall has been cleared-down
 * by the PSAP or by taf_ecall_End(), then a user can terminate eCall registration anytime after
 * T9 but before T10 expiration by calling the taf_ecall_TerminateRegistration() API.
 *
 * The taf_ecall_SetNadClearDownFallbackTime() API is used to set the time value of a
 * <em>clear down fallback timer</em> which starts when an eCall connects, so that if the NAD does not receive a clear
 * down indication from network or a clear down message (AL-ACK) from the PSAP during an ecall and then
 * automatically triggers an eCall end upon expiration of the timer.
 *
 * The taf_ecall_SetNadMinNetworkRegistrationTime() API is used to set the time value of a
 * <em>minimum network registration timer</em> which starts right after an eCall ends, so that the NAD shall remain
 * registered on the serving network after an eCall ends and automatically receive calls from the PSAP,
 * and then automatically deregisters from the network upon expiration of the timer.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_timer_state NAD eCall HLAP timer state
 *
 * The taf_ecall_GetHlapTimerState() API is used to get the timer status and elapsed time based on HLAP timer type.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_redial_configuration NAD eCall initial failed
 *
 * The dial parameters for a failed initial call in the Europe regulatory eCall system can be set using the following
 * APIs. Note that this configuration is not persistent after modem reboots. The range of the number of redial attempts
 * is [1,10] and the default value is 10. The default dial intervals between dial attempts are follows and users can
 * set the initial dial interval to be equal to or greater than the default value.
 * - 1st redial interval: the default value is 5 seconds and the supported range is from 5 to 30 seconds.
 * - 2nd-10th redial intervals: the default value is 30 seconds and the supported range is from 30 to 60 seconds.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_SetInitialDialAttempts() -- Sets the number of dial attempts.
 * - taf_ecall_SetInitialDialIntervalBetweenDialAttempts() -- Sets the dial interval value between dial attempts.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_concurrency eCall concurrency
 *
 * If another application wants to use the eCall service when a session is already active, the
 * taf_ecall_StartManual(), taf_ecall_StartAutomatic(), taf_ecall_StartTest(), taf_ecall_StartPrivate()
 * functions will return
 * @ref LE_BUSY error and the eCall session which is in progress will not be interrupted or disturbed.
 * The application may get the session progress 'state' using API like @ref taf_ecall_GetState() and
 * @ref taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler().
 * A manual eCall cannot disturb an automatic eCall and vice-versa.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_msd Minimum Set of Data (MSD)
 *
 * The dynamic values of MSD can be written with the following APIs.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPosition() -- Sets the position of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPositionN1() -- Sets the position delta N-1 for MSD transmission.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPositionN2() -- Sets the position delta N-2 for MSD transmission.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPassengersCount() -- Sets the number of passengers.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdAdditionalData() -- Sets the additional data of the the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_ResetMsdAdditionalData() -- Resets the additional data of the the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdEuroNCAPLocationOfImpact() -- Sets the location of impact for Euro NCAP additional data of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdEuroNCAPRolloverDetected() -- Sets the rollover detected for Euro NCAP additional data of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_ResetMsdEuroNCAPLocationOfImpact() -- Resets the rollover detected for Euro NCAP additional data of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdEuroNCAPIIDeltaV() -- Sets the IIDeltaV for Euro NCAP additional data of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdTimeStamp() -- Sets the MSD timestamp as the given value.
 * - taf_ecall_ResetMsdTimeStamp() -- Resets the MSD timestamp to the system time before session start.
 *
 * The MSD is automatically encoded with the previous MSD values set earlier.
 *
 * @b WARNING: The above functions may return a @ref LE_DUPLICATE error when MSD has already been imported
 *             using the taf_ecall_ImportMsd() API.
 *
 * The MSD transmission mode can be set and retrieved using the following APIs.
 *  - taf_ecall_SetMsdTxMode(): Not supported on this platform.
 *  - taf_ecall_GetMsdTxMode(): Not supported on this platform.
 *
 * The transmission modes can be:
 * - @ref TAF_ECALL_TX_MODE_PUSH -- MSD has been pushed by the IVS
 * - @ref TAF_ECALL_TX_MODE_PULL -- MSD has been sent when asked by the PSAP
 *
 * An application can import an existing MSD using the taf_ecall_ImportMsd() API.
 * The existing MSD must follow the requirements presented in the "EN15722:2020" publication (this
 * publication is prepared by Technical Committee CEN/TC 278 "Intelligent Transport Systems") or import
 * an MSD with maximum length of 255 bytes for Private eCall over IMS.
 *
 * @b WARNING: The imported MSD does not consider the values provided by the
 *             taf_ecall_SetMsdXxx() APIs. It overwrites any MSD imported or encoded previously.
 *
 * @b WARNING: The imported MSD may overwrite the control flags (automatic and test eCall) set by
 *             taf_ecall_StartXxx() APIs (Manual, Automatic, Test). The user app is responsible for the
 *             proper settings.
 *
 * The encoded MSD provided by taf_ecall_ImportMsd() API or taf_ecall_SetMsdXxx() API can be fetched with
 * the taf_ecall_ExportMsd() API.
 *
 * @b NOTE: The user application should perform the MSD transmission by using taf_ecall_SendMsd() when the
 * @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_MSD_UPDATE_REQ event arrives.
 * The MSD may be modified before calling taf_ecall_SendMsd() by the e_ecall_ImportMsd() API
 * or the taf_ecall_SetMsdXxx() APIs.
 *
 * @section c_taf_ecall_outgoing Starting an emergency call
 *
 * An emergency call can be started by using taf_ecall_StartAutomatic() with the ecallRef passed as
 * a parameter.
 * To get ECallRef we need to call taf_ecall_Create() with no parameters. This creates
 * an ECallRef object and returns it. Applicatons can cache the ECallRef for future use.
 * @verbatim
   static taf_ecall_CallRef_t ECallRef = taf_ecall_Create();
   if (!ECallRef)
   {
      le_result_t res = taf_ecall_StartAutomatic(ECallRef);
      LE_ASSERT(res == LE_OK);
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * Before the emergency call is started, an application registers a state change handler using
 * taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler(). Once the emergency call is established, the handler will be
 * called indicating it's now connected. If the state of the emergency call changes, then the
 * handler will be called with the new state.
 * @verbatim
   taf_ecall_StateChangeHandlerRef = taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler((taf_ecall_StateChangeHandlerFunc_t) tafECallStateHandler, NULL);
   @endverbatim
 *
 * To end an emergency call, an application can use taf_ecall_End().
 *
 * Applications must use taf_ecall_Delete() to release @ref taf_ecall_CallRef_t emergency call
 * reference object when it is no longer used.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_usage_flow Typical application call flow
 *
 * @rstblock
 * .. image:: /rst/flow_diagrams/eCall_usage_flow.jpg
 * @endrst
 *
 * eCall apps can use the TelAF eCall service to start an eCall with a PSAP, enable conversation over a voice channel,
 * and end the eCall.
 *
 * #1 -- Create an eCall session and get the eCall reference which will be used to make an eCall with PSAP.
 *
 * #2 -- Register the state change handler to get notifications from the TelAF eCall service when the eCall state gets changed.
 *
 * #3 -- Construct MSD message, including position information from the GNSS service, vehicle information, passenger count, etc.
 *
 * #4 -- Start an eCall via the eCall Service. The eCall service will initiate a corresponding eCall to PSAP. After this, the
 *       state change handler will be notified that the eCall state is DIALING and then ALERTING which means that the eCall
 *       successfully reached the PSAP.
 *
 *       After the eCall is answered by the PSAP, the eCall state changes to ACTIVE and in MSD Pull mode, the eCall Service
 *       gets a state indication TAF_STATE_MSD_UPDATE_REQ from the PSAP to receive MSD.
 *       Without this state indication, as of now, the client application should update MSD to the NAD (i.e., modem) by calling
 *       the taf_ecall_SendMsd() API. Later, when the NAD gets an indication from the PSAP in pull mode, NAD will use the updated
 *       MSD and send it to the PSAP.
 *
 * #5 -- Start sending encoded MSD via the eCall Service to the PSAP. The eCall state becomes TAF_STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_STARTED and the
 *       TAF_STATE_LL_ACK_RECEIVED.
 *
 *       After PSAP successfully receives the MSD, the eCall state changes to TAF_STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_SUCCESS and the state change
 *       hander will be notified.
 *
 *       Call active: The eCall app might need to stay active to reserve a voice call channel to enable the passenger to talk with the PSAP.
 *
 * #6 -- When the conversation is finished, the eCall app can end the call using the eCall Service API. This will send the BYE signal to the PSAP.
 *       After the eCall is successfully ended, the eCall state will change to ENDED and the state change handler will be notified of the same.
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

USETYPES taf_types.api;
USETYPES taf_sim.api;
REFERENCE Call;

/**
 * Support for legacy operational modes.
 */
DEFINE TX_MODE_PULL = 0;
DEFINE TX_MODE_PUSH = 1;
DEFINE MAX_VIN_LENGTH  =  (17);
DEFINE MAX_VIN_BYTES  =  MAX_VIN_LENGTH + (1);
DEFINE MAX_OID_LENGTH  =  (8);
DEFINE MAX_DATA_LENGTH  =  (94);
DEFINE MAX_MSD_LENGTH = (255);
DEFINE CONTENT_TYPE_MAX_LENGTH = (128);
DEFINE ACCEPT_INFO_MAX_LENGTH = (128);
DEFINE MAX_DIAL_ATTEMPTS_LENGTH = (10);

/**
 *  Operational modes.
 */
ENUM OpMode
{
    MODE_NORMAL,                   ///< eCall normal mode.
    MODE_ECALL,                    ///< eCall only mode.
    MODE_FORCED_PERSISTENT_ONLY,   ///< Persistent eCall only mode and is deprecated.
    NONE                           ///< Invalid mode and is deprecated.
};

/**
 *  MSD transmission modes per the eCall MSD standard.
 */
ENUM MsdTransmissionMode
{
    MSD_TX_MODE_PULL,  ///< Pull mode; modem/host waits for MSD request from PSAP to send MSD.
    MSD_TX_MODE_PUSH   ///< Push mode; modem/host sends MSD to PSAP after the eCall is connected.
};

/**
 *  Vehicle classes per the European eCall MSD standard.
 *
 */
ENUM MsdVehicleType
{
    PASSENGER_VEHICLE_CLASS_M1,            ///< Passenger vehicle (Class M1)
    BUSES_AND_COACHES_CLASS_M2,            ///< Buses and coaches (Class M2)
    BUSES_AND_COACHES_CLASS_M3,            ///< Buses and coaches (Class M3)
    LIGHT_COMMERCIAL_VEHICLES_CLASS_N1,    ///< Light commercial vehicles (Class N1)
    HEAVY_DUTY_VEHICLES_CLASS_N2,          ///< Heavy duty vehicles (Class N2)
    HEAVY_DUTY_VEHICLES_CLASS_N3,          ///< Heavy duty vehicles (Class N3)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L1E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L1e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L2E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L2e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L3E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L3e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L4E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L4e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L5E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L5e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L6E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L6e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L7E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L7e)
    TRAILERS_CLASS_O,                      ///< Trailers (Class O)
    AGRI_VEHICLES_CLASS_R,                 ///< Agricultural vehicles (Class R)
    AGRI_VEHICLES_CLASS_S,                 ///< Agricultural vehicles (Class S)
    AGRI_VEHICLES_CLASS_T,                 ///< Agricultural vehicles (Class T)
    OFF_ROAD_VEHICLES_G,                   ///< Off-road vehicles (Class G)
    SPECIAL_PURPOSE_MOTOR_CARAVAN_CLASS_SA,///< Special purpose motor caravan (Class SA)
    SPECIAL_PURPOSE_ARMOURED_VEHICLE_CLASS_SB,///< Special purpose armoured vehicle (Class SB)
    SPECIAL_PURPOSE_AMBULANCE_CLASS_SC,    ///< Special purpose ambulance (Class SC)
    SPECIAL_PURPOSE_HEARSE_CLASS_SD,       ///< Special purpose hearse (Class SD)
    OTHER_VEHICLE_CLASS,                   ///< Other vehicle class
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Propulsion storage type bitmask
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BITMASK PropulsionStorageType
{
    PROP_TYPE_GASOLINE_TANK,         ///< Indicates the presence of a gasoline tank in the vehicle.
    PROP_TYPE_DIESEL_TANK,           ///< Indicates the presence of diesel tank in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_COMPRESSED_NATURALGAS, ///< Indicates the presence of CNG in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_PROPANE_GAS,           ///< Indicates the presence of liquid propane in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_ELECTRIC,              ///< Indicates the presence of electronic storage in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_HYDROGEN,              ///< Indicates the presence of hydrogen Storage in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_OTHER,                 ///< Indicates the presence of other types of storage in the vehicle
};

/**
 *  Vehicle location of impact per Euro NCAP.
 *
 */
ENUM IILocations
{
    LOI_UNKNOWN,
    LOI_NONE,
    LOI_FRONT,
    LOI_REAR,
    LOI_DRIVERSIDE,
    LOI_NONDRIVERSIDE,
    LOI_OTHER
};

/**
 *  eCall states.
 */
ENUM State
{
    STATE_UNKNOWN,                            ///< Unknown eCall state.
    STATE_ALERTING,                           ///< Alerting call; MO call only.
    STATE_ACTIVE,                             ///< Active eCall.
    STATE_IDLE,                               ///< Not supported.
    STATE_WAITING_PSAP_START_IND,             ///< Not supported.
    STATE_PSAP_START_RECEIVED,                ///< Send MSD (start) is received and sync is locked during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_STARTED,           ///< In-band MSD transmission started.
    STATE_LLNACK_RECEIVED,                    ///< Not supported.
    STATE_LL_ACK_RECEIVED,                    ///< Link-Layer Acknowledgement (LL-ACK) is received during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_SUCCESS,           ///< In-band MSD transmission succeeded.
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_FAILED,            ///< In-band MSD transmission failed.
    STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_POSITIVE,            ///< Application-Layer Acknowledgement (positive) is received during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_CLEAR_DOWN,          ///< Application-Layer Acknowledgement (cleardown) is received during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_ENDED,                              ///< Call stopped.
    STATE_RESET,                              ///< Not supported.
    STATE_COMPLETED,                          ///< Not supported.
    STATE_FAILED,                             ///< If the modem crashes or reboots while an eCall is in progress, the system will report
                                              ///< a "modem unavailable" event to eCall service. This state indicates that the modem is
                                              ///< temporarily inaccessible and cannot continue the eCall operation.
    STATE_END_OF_REDIAL_PERIOD,               ///< Ended call of the redial period.
    STATE_T2_EXPIRED,                         ///< T2 timer expired.
    STATE_TIMEOUT_T3,                         ///< Not  supported.
    STATE_T5_EXPIRED,                         ///< T5 Timer expired.
    STATE_T6_EXPIRED,                         ///< T6 Timer expired.
    STATE_T7_EXPIRED,                         ///< T7 Timer expired.
    STATE_T9_EXPIRED,                         ///< T9 Timer expired.
    STATE_T10_EXPIRED,                        ///< T10 Timer expired.
    STATE_DIALING,                            ///< Outgoing call.
    STATE_NACK_OUT_OF_ORDER,                  ///< Out of order NACK message detected during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_ACK_OUT_OF_ORDER,                   ///< Out of order ACK message detected during in-band MSD transmission.
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_STARTED,   ///< Out-band MSD transmission started in NG eCall.
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_SUCCESS,   ///< Out-band MSD transmission succeeded in NG eCall or private eCall.
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_FAILURE,   ///< Out-band MSD transmission failed in NG eCall or private eCall.
    STATE_MSD_UPDATE_REQ,                     ///< Notify request from PSAP for MSD update.
    STATE_T2_STARTED,                         ///< T2 Timer started.
    STATE_T5_STARTED,                         ///< T5 Timer started.
    STATE_T6_STARTED,                         ///< T6 Timer started.
    STATE_T7_STARTED,                         ///< T7 Timer started.
    STATE_T9_STARTED,                         ///< T9 Timer started.
    STATE_T10_STARTED,                        ///< T10 Timer started.
    STATE_T2_STOPPED,                         ///< T2 Timer stopped.
    STATE_T5_STOPPED,                         ///< T5 Timer stopped.
    STATE_T6_STOPPED,                         ///< T6 Timer stopped.
    STATE_T7_STOPPED,                         ///< T7 Timer stopped.
    STATE_T9_STOPPED,                         ///< T9 Timer stopped.
    STATE_T10_STOPPED,                        ///< T10 Timer stopped.
    STATE_INCOMING,                           ///< Incoming eCall.
    STATE_LL_NACK_DUE_TO_T7_EXPIRY,           ///< Link-Layer Acknowledgement (LL-NACK) is received during in-band MSD transmission due to expiry of T7 Timer.
    STATE_T9_RESUMED,                         ///< T9 Timer resumed.
    STATE_T10_RESUMED                         ///< T10 Timer resumed.
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Recently terminated call end reasons (normally ended or failed).
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM TerminationReason
{
   REASON_UNOBTAINABLE_NUMBER = 1,
   REASON_NO_ROUTE_TO_DESTINATION = 3,
   REASON_CHANNEL_UNACCEPTABLE = 6,
   REASON_OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING = 8,
   REASON_NORMAL = 16,
   REASON_BUSY = 17,
   REASON_NO_USER_RESPONDING = 18,
   REASON_NO_ANSWER_FROM_USER = 19,
   REASON_NOT_REACHABLE = 20,
   REASON_CALL_REJECTED = 21,
   REASON_NUMBER_CHANGED = 22,
   REASON_PREEMPTION = 25,
   REASON_DESTINATION_OUT_OF_ORDER = 27,
   REASON_INVALID_NUMBER_FORMAT = 28,
   REASON_FACILITY_REJECTED = 29,
   REASON_RESP_TO_STATUS_ENQUIRY = 30,
   REASON_NORMAL_UNSPECIFIED = 31,
   REASON_CONGESTION = 34,
   REASON_NETWORK_OUT_OF_ORDER = 38,
   REASON_TEMPORARY_FAILURE = 41,
   REASON_SWITCHING_EQUIPMENT_CONGESTION = 42,
   REASON_ACCESS_INFORMATION_DISCARDED = 43,
   REASON_REQUESTED_CIRCUIT_OR_CHANNEL_NOT_AVAILABLE = 44,
   REASON_RESOURCES_UNAVAILABLE_OR_UNSPECIFIED = 47,
   REASON_QOS_UNAVAILABLE = 49,
   REASON_REQUESTED_FACILITY_NOT_SUBSCRIBED = 50,
   REASON_INCOMING_CALLS_BARRED_WITHIN_CUG = 55,
   REASON_BEARER_CAPABILITY_NOT_AUTHORIZED = 57,
   REASON_BEARER_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE = 58,
   REASON_SERVICE_OPTION_NOT_AVAILABLE = 63,
   REASON_BEARER_SERVICE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 65,
   REASON_ACM_LIMIT_EXCEEDED = 68,
   REASON_REQUESTED_FACILITY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 69,
   REASON_ONLY_DIGITAL_INFORMATION_BEARER_AVAILABLE = 70,
   REASON_SERVICE_OR_OPTION_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 79,
   REASON_INVALID_TRANSACTION_IDENTIFIER = 81,
   REASON_USER_NOT_MEMBER_OF_CUG = 87,
   REASON_INCOMPATIBLE_DESTINATION = 88,
   REASON_INVALID_TRANSIT_NW_SELECTION = 91,
   REASON_SEMANTICALLY_INCORRECT_MESSAGE = 95,
   REASON_INVALID_MANDATORY_INFORMATION = 96,
   REASON_MESSAGE_TYPE_NON_IMPLEMENTED = 97,
   REASON_MESSAGE_TYPE_NOT_COMPATIBLE_WITH_PROTOCOL_STATE = 98,
   REASON_INFORMATION_ELEMENT_NON_EXISTENT = 99,
   REASON_CONDITIONAL_IE_ERROR = 100,
   REASON_MESSAGE_NOT_COMPATIBLE_WITH_PROTOCOL_STATE = 101,
   REASON_RECOVERY_ON_TIMER_EXPIRED = 102,
   REASON_PROTOCOL_ERROR_UNSPECIFIED = 111,
   REASON_INTERWORKING_UNSPECIFIED = 127,
   REASON_CALL_BARRED = 240,
   REASON_FDN_BLOCKED = 241,
   REASON_IMSI_UNKNOWN_IN_VLR = 242,
   REASON_IMEI_NOT_ACCEPTED = 243,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_USSD = 244,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_SS = 245,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_DIAL = 246,
   REASON_CDMA_LOCKED_UNTIL_POWER_CYCLE = 1000,
   REASON_CDMA_DROP = 1001,
   REASON_CDMA_INTERCEPT = 1002,
   REASON_CDMA_REORDER = 1003,
   REASON_CDMA_SO_REJECT = 1004,
   REASON_CDMA_RETRY_ORDER = 1005,
   REASON_CDMA_ACCESS_FAILURE = 1006,
   REASON_CDMA_PREEMPTED = 1007,
   REASON_CDMA_NOT_EMERGENCY = 1008,
   REASON_CDMA_ACCESS_BLOCKED = 1009,
   REASON_ERROR_UNSPECIFIED = 0xffff
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * eCall type
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM Type
{
    TYPE_UNKNOWN,
    TYPE_TEST,
    TYPE_AUTO,
    TYPE_MANUAL,
    TYPE_PRIVATE
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * HLAP timer status
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM HlapTimerStatus {
    TIMER_STATUS_UNKNOWN,    ///< Unknown.
    TIMER_STATUS_INACTIVE,   ///< eCall HLAP timer has not started or it has stopped/expired.
    TIMER_STATUS_ACTIVE      ///< eCall HLAP timer has started but not yet stopped/expired.
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * HLAP timer type
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM HlapTimerType {
    TIMER_TYPE_UNKNOWN,      ///< Unknown timer
    TIMER_TYPE_T2 = 2,       ///< T2 timer.
    TIMER_TYPE_T9 = 9,       ///< T9 timer.
    TIMER_TYPE_T10 = 10      ///< T10 timer.
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for changes in eCall state.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER StateChangeHandler
(
    Call  ecallRef IN,    ///< Emergency call reference.
    State state    IN     ///< Emergency call state.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * eCall state change event handler.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT StateChange
(
    StateChangeHandler handler ///< State change handler for emergency calls.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Creates an eCall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - Reference to the emergency call.
 *      - NULL if the emergency call can not be created.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION Call Create
(
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Releases (frees) a call reference according to the given eCall reference.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION Delete
(
    Call ecallRef IN   ///< Emergency call reference.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Switches to eCall only mode according to the given phone ID.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ForceOnlyMode
(
     uint8              phoneId  IN     ///< Phone ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Switches to persistent eCall Only mode according to the given phone ID.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 * @deprecated This function is deprecated. taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode should be used instead.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ForcePersistentOnlyMode
(
     uint8              phoneId  IN     ///< Phone ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Exits eCall Only mode and switches to Normal mode according to the given phone ID.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ExitOnlyMode
(
     uint8              phoneId  IN     ///< Phone ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the ecall operating mode according to the given phone ID.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetConfiguredOperationMode
(
    uint8             phoneId  IN,     ///< Phone ID.
    OpMode             opMode  OUT     ///< Operating mode.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Sets the MSD version.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 * @b NOTE: Currently, only MSD version 2 and 3 are supported.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdVersion
(
    uint32 msdVersion IN
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Gets the MSD version.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Invalid parameters.
 *
 * @b NOTE: Currently, only MSD version 2 and 3 are supported.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetMsdVersion
(
    uint32 msdVer OUT    ///< MSD version as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Sets the vehicle type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetVehicleType
(
    MsdVehicleType vehType   IN     ///< Vehicle type.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Get vehicle type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Invalid parameters.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetVehicleType
(
    MsdVehicleType vehType   OUT  ///< Vehicle type as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
